-- title:
--   Switcheroo First Term Close
-- statement:
--   **The first positive term is close to the common center by M self consistency.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and assume the switcheroo self-consistency relation for `M` with error `omega` over uniform slice questions. Writing $T_1$ for the first positive term and $C$ for the middle-sandwich common term, the two transfer estimates give
--
--   $$
--   \left|T_1-C\right|\le2\sqrt{\omega}.
--   $$
--
--   The first-term and target center rewrites identify the endpoints as left- and middle-sandwich averages. The bipartite self-consistency conversion and the average absolute-value inequality then provide the displayed two-root error bound.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcheroo_first_term_close`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
